  rAs: {la: "", en: "", strip: 1, lines: [

  ], adv: [
    {"m": "mc", "r": "On Sundays, when the Hour before Mass is finished, the priest, deacon and subdeacon come to the sanctuary in albs with stoles and maniples (if there is to be a procession, the priest in a silk cope and the ministers in dalmatics), the acolytes going before. The deacon stands with the senior acolyte at the priest’s right, the subdeacon with the junior at his left; all bow profoundly (or genuflect) before the altar.", "ref": ["ministri-ii-1"]},
    {"m": "c", "r": "The senior acolyte brings the water, the deacon hands the sprinkler, and as the cantors begin Asperges me the priest sprinkles the high altar (not too much), then the deacon, subdeacon and acolytes, the Master of the Order if present, the cantors on Doubles, and the brethren, beginning on the right; after the clerics the lay brothers, then the seculars in choir. The same order is kept for the peace and the incensing.", "ref": ["ministri-ii-2"]},
    {"m": "m", "r": "The priest sprinkles the altar, the ministers and the people.", "ref": ["ministri-ii-2"]},
    {"m": "c", "if": "mo", "r": "The Master of the Order is sprinkled next after the ministers and acolytes, before the cantors and the brethren.", "ref": ["ministri-ii-2"]},
    {"m": "mc", "r": "When the antiphon is finished, standing before the sanctuary steps as at the beginning, he says Ostende nobis, Dominus vobiscum, Oremus and the prayer Exaudi nos; then the ministers return to the sacristy (and, if there is a procession, it follows, after which the priest exchanges the cope for the chasuble).", "ref": ["ministri-ii-3", "ministri-ii-4"]}
  ]},
  rIn: {la: "", en: "", strip: 1, lines: [

  ], adv: [
    {"m": "ls", "r": "At the Epistle corner he begins the Introit in a clear and audible voice; at Gloria Patri he bows his head a little towards the cross (in Masses for the Dead there is no Gloria Patri, and the Requiem aeternam is repeated after the verse); then he repeats the Introit as far as the verse.", "ref": ["modus-ii-1", "varia-iv-1"]},
    {"m": "mc", "r": "All come together at the book, opened by the deacon (who turns the pages and points out what is to be said), and standing at the priest’s right in order of rank say the Introit and the Kyrie with him; they do not kneel at Salve sancta parens.", "ref": ["ministri-iii-4"]},
    {"m": "mc", "r": "Then the deacon stands behind the priest and the subdeacon behind the deacon; the acolytes stand below the sanctuary steps (or in the first stalls of the choir), and never go up to the top step. During the Canon they stand at the deacon’s right and left, in the form of a cross.", "ref": ["ministri-iii-5"]}
  ]},
  rKy: {la: "", en: "", strip: 1, lines: [

  ], adv: [
    {"m": "l", "r": "He says the Kyrie eleison alternately with the server.", "ref": ["modus-ii-1", "varia-vi-4"]},
    {"m": "mc", "r": "On Sundays, and on Doubles and above, the priest, deacon and subdeacon may sit at the Epistle side (the deacon at the priest’s left, the subdeacon at the deacon’s left, the acolytes on a lower bench). The acolytes spread a small cloth over their knees, and one of them takes it up at the last Kyrie eleison, beginning with the priest and kissing his hand.", "ref": ["ministri-iii-6"]},
    {"m": "mc", "if": "nogl", "r": "When the Gloria is not said (from Septuagesima to Easter), the subdeacon fetches the chalice from the sacristy during the Kyrie, as is done during the Gloria on other days.", "ref": ["ministri-iv-2"]}
  ]},
  rGl: {la: "", en: "", strip: 1, lines: [

  ], adv: [
    {"m": "l", "r": "The last Kyrie said, he goes with hands joined to the middle of the altar. At Gloria he lays his hands extended on the altar; at in excelsis he raises them; at Deo he joins them and bows his head; then he returns to the Epistle corner and continues it at the book with hands joined. He bows his head at Adoramus te, Gratias agimus tibi, Jesu Christe, suscipe deprecationem nostram, and again at Jesu Christe.", "ref": ["modus-ii-2"]},
    {"m": "s", "r": "The last Kyrie sung, he goes to the middle of the altar and intones the Gloria, with the gestures of the Low Mass (hands laid on the altar at Gloria, raised at in excelsis, joined at Deo, with a bow); then he goes to the Epistle corner and continues it at the book, bowing at Adoramus te, Gratias agimus tibi, Jesu Christe and Suscipe deprecationem nostram.", "ref": ["modus-ii-2", "ministri-iv-1"]},
    {"m": "ls", "if": "exp", "r": "The Sacrament is exposed: he genuflects on one knee as he comes to the middle for the Gloria and again as he leaves it.", "ref": ["varia-ii-4"]},
    {"m": "mc", "r": "All rise, stand before the middle of the altar and bow profoundly; the priest goes up and intones the Gloria. Then all go together to the Epistle corner and continue it with him, standing at his right; when it is said, the priest and deacon stand until the community has finished it. The ministers pass behind, never between, those of higher rank.", "ref": ["ministri-iv-1"]},
    {"m": "mc", "r": "Meanwhile on Sundays and Doubles the subdeacon, an acolyte going before with the wine and water, goes to the sacristy, puts on a clean veil over his shoulders, and brings the prepared chalice raised before his breast; they bow profoundly in the middle; he sets the chalice on the veil spread on the Epistle corner, and the acolyte puts the cruets in the niche or on a bench.", "ref": ["ministri-iv-2"]}
  ]},
